From: Armada contributors <noreply@armada-os.org>
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: qcom: sc8280xp: match Pocket Duo speaker slot width

The Duo AW88166 firmware configures I2SCTRL1 for 32-bit slots and a
64-fs bit clock. The existing S16_LE backend supplies only 32-fs BCLK,
leaving both amplifiers stuck at SYSST 0x0011 during startup.

Use S32_LE on the Duo primary MI2S playback backend. The existing
hw_params callback then supplies 3.072 MHz BCLK at 48 kHz, matching
the amplifier configuration without changing its firmware or driver.
Both amplifiers reach SYSST 0x0311 with this backend format. Together with
the matching S32_LE speaker topology and q6apm playback support, speaker
output was confirmed after a clean boot on the Duo. Headphone and capture
formats remain unchanged.

Register definitions: https://github.com/awinic-driver/aw883xx/blob/main/aw883xx_pid_2066_reg.h

---
--- a/sound/soc/qcom/sc8280xp.c
+++ b/sound/soc/qcom/sc8280xp.c
@@ -143,7 +143,13 @@
 	struct snd_mask *fmt = hw_param_mask(params, SNDRV_PCM_HW_PARAM_FORMAT);
 
 	rate->min = rate->max = 48000;
-	snd_mask_set_format(fmt, SNDRV_PCM_FORMAT_S16_LE);
+	if (of_machine_is_compatible("retroidpocket,duo") &&
+	    cpu_dai->id == PRIMARY_MI2S_RX) {
+		snd_mask_none(fmt);
+		snd_mask_set_format(fmt, SNDRV_PCM_FORMAT_S32_LE);
+	} else {
+		snd_mask_set_format(fmt, SNDRV_PCM_FORMAT_S16_LE);
+	}
 	channels->min = 2;
 	channels->max = 2;
 	switch (cpu_dai->id) {
